<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Wanga Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1926 CE (approx.) · capital Elureko</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The only centralised kingdom among the Luhya of western Kenya, whose king Mumia became a key ally of British colonial expansion.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Wanga traditions say the kingdom was founded around the mid-17th century by Wanga, a prince who had migrated from the area of Tiriki or further west and established a royal line among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luhya-people">Luhya</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumias">Mumias</a> area. The capital lay at Elureko, near today's Mumias.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The nabongo (king) ruled with clan elders and a royal council over a farming people, and used alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maasai-people">Maasai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalenjin-people">Kalenjin</a> warriors to raid and dominate neighbours. In the 19th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> and Arab caravans used Wanga as a base. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabongo-mumia">Nabongo Mumia</a> (r. 1882 to 1949) welcomed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imperial-british-east-africa-company">Imperial British East Africa Company</a> and helped British expansion across western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kenya">Kenya</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The British made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabongo-mumia">Mumia</a> paramount chief of much of western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kenya">Kenya</a>, but in 1926 his authority was reduced to an honorary position, ending Wanga's role as a governing kingdom. The town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumias">Mumias</a> bears his name, and the title of nabongo survives as a cultural office.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/wanga-kingdom.jpg" alt="Wanga Kingdom" width="320" height="352"><figcaption>Image: NordNordWest · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kakamega_County_in_Kenya.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1926 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Elureko</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mumia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwanga</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Kenya</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Wanga, Wanga</dd></dl></aside></div>

